# Next.js Server Actions Best Practices

- Use Server Actions for trusted server-side mutations from forms and UI workflows.
- Co-locate simple actions with the page/component; extract shared actions to dedicated server files.
- Validate all inputs on the server (prefer schema-based validation) before DB or API writes.
- Enforce authorization inside each action; never rely only on client checks.
- Return typed success/error states for recoverable UI errors; throw only for unexpected failures.
- Revalidate affected paths/tags (`revalidatePath`/`revalidateTag`) after mutations to keep UI consistent.
- Keep actions idempotent where possible and log meaningful context for operational debugging.
